[["text","LESSON 10 / 31 • ORIGINAL CHECKLIST"],["heading","10. Adjacency lists and matrices"],["text","English: Two ways to represent graph connections."],["sinhala","","සිංහල: Graph connections list එකකින් Jහහෝ matrix එකකින් නිරූපණය කරන්න පුළුවෙන්.",444],["text","Real-world example: Friend connections"],["code","A: B"],["code","B: A      matrix: [0 1; 1 0]"],["heading","Java example / illustration"],["code","int[][] matrix = {{0,1},{1,0}};\nSystem.out.println(matrix[0][1]); // 1"],["heading","Complexity and trade-offs"],["text","List space O(V+E); matrix O(V²); matrix edge check O(1)."],["heading","Interview question"],["heading","Which is better for sparse graphs?"],["text","Adjacency lists usually use less memory."],["heading","Quick practice"],["text","Explain this concept aloud, trace the example, and describe when you would choose this"],["text","structure over an alternative."]]